From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Vicory <dvicory@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 10:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(workspaces): pin workers to broker runtime identity

Broker pre-spawn activated a task-run environment, but the worker inherited no
HERMES_BROKER_ENVIRONMENT_KEY and derived a separate conversation environment.
The worker could create and verify an artifact that the authoritative handoff
workspace could not see, causing capture to report that output changed.

Pass the pre-spawn key through the shared worker environment contract so every
terminal and file surface uses the activated task workspace. Invoke required
finalization hooks without swallowing their broker errors, and notify both the
subscriber and originating session when repeated blocks route work to triage.

Add regressions for runtime identity propagation, required-hook failures, and
block-loop triage delivery.
---
--- a/hermes_cli/worker_lanes.py
+++ b/hermes_cli/worker_lanes.py
@@ -173,6 +173,12 @@
     if getattr(task, "workspace_kind", "") == "broker":
         env["HERMES_WORKSPACE_MODE"] = "broker"
         env["HERMES_BROKER_WORKSPACE"] = "/workspace"
+        from tools.environments.gondolin import broker_environment_key
+
+        # The workspace pre-spawn hook activates this exact broker key. Pass
+        # it into the worker so terminal and file surfaces use that task-run
+        # workspace rather than deriving a separate conversation environment.
+        env["HERMES_BROKER_ENVIRONMENT_KEY"] = broker_environment_key(task.id)
     if workspace:
         env["HERMES_KANBAN_WORKSPACE"] = workspace
     # Pin the shared umbrella root + DB + workspaces root the dispatcher
